    "title": "New ATLAS CTE Center name approved for Ector County ISD - NewsBreak",
    "text": "17 hours ago The Ector County ISD Board of Trustees has officially named the district’s new Career & Technical Education high school the ATLAS CTE Center , short for Advancing Trades, Learning, and Skills . The facility, funded by Bond 2023 , will serve about 400 full-time high school students and provide CTE courses for roughly 2,000 more across the district when it opens in 2027 .\nThe board also reviewed progress on several bond projects, including new middle and high school facilities, the Ag Farm, and the Transportation Facility. About one-third of bond funds (around $141 million) remain available for ongoing work. Trustees also approved updates to facility naming policies and several construction contracts.\nResidents can follow project updates at www.ecisdbond.com .\nMore Info: School board approves name for new CTE facility fu...",
